{"id": "EUVD-2026-103966", "enisaUuid": "b0aa53a4-25e9-3171-b0e1-90ba3857b2cf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: vgic: Take a refcount on IRQs referenced by last_lr_irq\n\nReferencing the last interrupt inserted in an LR is rather fragile, as\nthis interrupt can vanish if a concurrently unmapped LPI.\n\nSolve this by bumping up the refcount on the interrupt when populating\nlast_lr_irq, and drop it at vgic_prune_ap_list() time, when LPIs are\nbeing reclaimed.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:24:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8b25393d16a5ca8df907bd7ee1ff2e9d85678b3c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/19bc5d79ece613f242b5ec03921a3b465321bfed"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98712", "GHSA-fqwg-6qxx-rx2q"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02b27f20-a9c3-3dde-b2a5-66414787e4a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6da5e537f5afe091658e846da1949d7e557d2ade <8b25393d16a5ca8df907bd7ee1ff2e9d85678b3c"}, {"id": "11650d80-568d-38bc-8081-08bc38edf892", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd28ca4c27ed5929f61bbed8a967c20519facb88"}, {"id": "308243bc-3c78-3c39-a3fa-aab17a0e4451", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "63e7f364-ca6a-33b6-b6fe-65e9a8a520b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "8a767f4f-d272-3158-bc37-2045dd8ea628", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "aa4a3015-6c6e-333f-ad07-ee692dc74802", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6da5e537f5afe091658e846da1949d7e557d2ade <19bc5d79ece613f242b5ec03921a3b465321bfed"}, {"id": "ce60e13f-0bfe-30b5-ac15-c5f60bebe250", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vend